<%
/* ============================================================================
   Primary navigation.

   The nav is DATA, rendered by one loop. Every destination is declared once,
   in NAV below, and three things read from that single list: the sidebar, the
   command palette at the bottom of this file, and the active-state resolver.
   A link therefore cannot exist in one and be missing from another, and the
   icon / label / badge / tooltip contract cannot drift between 34 hand
   written anchors the way it did before.

   ACTIVE STATE COMES FROM THE URL, NOT FROM A FLAG.
   Every /ai-seo/* route renders with active='aiseo', so a flag-based check lit
   up one item whichever of the /ai-seo pages you were actually on. Matching
   the real request path fixes them all at once, and every page added later,
   with no route needing to remember a key. It is also what lets the sections
   below be regrouped freely: nothing about active state or open state is
   declared twice, so moving a link between sections is a one-line change.

   The rule is longest-prefix wins, resolved once against the whole list:
   /keywords and /keywords/briefs both prefix-match /keywords/briefs, and only
   the longer should light up. A per-link startsWith would light both.

   Routes are unchanged. Every href is the same URL it was before, so
   bookmarks, analytics and muscle memory all still work.

   ICONS: a custom set drawn to one locked spec (24x24, stroke 1.5, round caps
   and joins). Deliberately not Lucide or Feather, whose defaults are a
   giveaway. Custom rather than an icon package because this app has no build
   step, and a webfont would flash unstyled glyphs on ~60 server-rendered
   pages.
   ============================================================================ */

